WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:10.576
CLARISSA WARD: This is the image
the Taliban want to project.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:15.414
Friendly and pious,
bringing peace and security.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:18.718
On the streets of Ghazni
city, Taliban official

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:21.721
Maulvi Mansour
Afghan goes from shop

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.858
to shop talking to the owners.

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.058
- [non-english speech].

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:28.160
CLARISSA WARD: He asks
how the security situation

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:31.130
is with the Taliban in charge?

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.131
- [non-english speech]

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.432
CLARISSA WARD: The
situation is good.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:36.068
Praise be to God, the man says.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:39.038
It may well be a
performance for our cameras,

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:41.907
but it is telling
the Taliban wants

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.310
to show they have changed.

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.712
When you're talking to
the men and some of them

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.748
don't have long
beards, are you saying

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.450
anything to them
about their beards,

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.418
or does it matter right now?

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.020
- [non-english speech]

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.955
CLARISSA WARD: We tell the
people that this is the prophet

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:59.091
Muhammad Sunnah, and
make them aware, he says,

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:01.761
but we don't want to force
the people to do this.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:02.929
- [non-english speech]

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:04.531
CLARISSA WARD: In another
part of the market,

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:08.234
the newly resurrected
much-feared religious police

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:13.606
are also keen to show they
are taking a lighter touch.

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.008
They gather the
shopkeepers to introduce

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:18.811
themselves and warn them
about the importance

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:19.913
of following the Sharia.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.714
- [non-english speech]

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:24.016
CLARISSA WARD: Make sure
your women cover themselves,

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:25.952
one Talib tells the crowd.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:29.989
They should not travel
without a close male relative.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:34.126
A man stands nearby casually
smoking a cigarette,

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:37.830
a punishable offense under
the previous Taliban regime,

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:40.867
but no one says a thing.

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:43.436
Back at their headquarters
at the Ministry

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:46.972
for the propagation of virtue
and prevention of vise,

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:49.042
the men are still settling in.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:51.610
- [non-english speech]

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.145
CLARISSA WARD: Up
until recently,

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:57.283
this was the Ministry for women.

00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.887
The man now in charge
seems leery of my presence

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.822
and refuses to meet my eye.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:03.956
- [non-english speech]

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:05.891
CLARISSA WARD: He says
their mission is to help

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:08.994
Afghans embrace Islamic rule.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.996
And what do you
do if they're not

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:14.834
following your
interpretation of Sharia law?

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.969
MAWLAVI ABDULLAH MOHAMMED:
[non-english speech]

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.238 line:8%
- We act with accordance
to Sharia law.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:22.174 line:8%
Firstly we inform
people about good deeds.

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:24.077 line:8%
We preach to them and
deliver the message

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.678 line:14%
to them in a nice way.

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:28.948 line:8%
The second time we
repeat it to them again.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:31.917
And the third time, we speak
to them slightly harshly.

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:34.554
CLARISSA WARD: If his words
sound like talking points,

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:35.788
that's because they are.

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.523
- [non-english speech]

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.124
CLARISSA WARD: As
we leave, he hands

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:42.595
us a newly issued
Taliban booklet outlining

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:45.198
the group's gentler approach.

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:48.401 line:8%
So he says that this book
contains the rules for how they

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.203 line:14%
should carry out their work.

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:53.906
But old habits die
hard, and back in Kabul,

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:58.210
it's clear not everyone is
following the new guidelines.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:02:59.846
It's badly bruised.

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.348
In a secure location,
Waheed shows

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:06.586
us the ugly marks left
behind after he says he was

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.154
whipped by Taliban fighters.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.489
- [non-english speech]

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:11.857
CLARISSA WARD: We've changed
his name for his protection.

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:13.859
He tells us three
fighters stopped

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:18.898
him at a busy traffic circle for
wearing western-style clothing.

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.701
They took him into a
Guard hut and demanded

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:22.869
to see his cell phone.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.703
- [non-english speech]

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:27.339
- I had photos in my
phone related to gays.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.676
Also, the clothes I was
wearing were a gay style.

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:31.744
- [non-english speech]

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.846
- They took me and
covered my mouth.

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:37.250
Two of them held each of my
hands, and the third hit me.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.352
First with a whip,
and then with a stick.

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.654
- [non-english speech]

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:42.822
CLARISSA WARD: What
reason did they

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.691
give for doing this to you?

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.426
- [non-english speech]

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:48.727
- When they were beating
me, they kept saying that I

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:51.097
was a gay, I should be killed.

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:52.331
- [non-english speech]

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.500
- They had very scary faces.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:57.070
They were enjoying beating me.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:00.673
CLARISSA WARD: That lurid
brutality was on full display

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:04.276
weeks earlier in the
Western city of Herat

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:08.581
when the bloodied bodies of four
men were hung in public for all

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:09.549
to see.

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:12.051
The Taliban said
they were kidnappers

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:14.354
killed during a raid.

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:16.989
On one man's chest,
a grim warning,

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:20.559
"Abductors will be
punished like this."

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.895
Remarkably many in
the crowd seemed

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:25.832
to approve of the
Taliban's medieval display.

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:26.832
- [non-english speech]

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:27.934
CLARISSA WARD:
"People are really

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:30.636
happy about this
decision." this man said,

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:33.239
"because people believe
that by doing this,

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:38.044
kidnapping can be removed
from this province."

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:41.814
In another grotesque display,
two alleged criminals,

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.717
their faces painted,
were humiliated

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:47.319
before a jeering crowd.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:51.590
Punishment the Taliban
favors for petty thieves.

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:54.427
After the corruption of
the former government,

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:57.229
the group has seized
on a frenzie desire

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.365
for swift justice.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:02.234
But they are savvy
enough to know how it

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:03.903
looks to the rest of the world.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.838
- [non-english speech]

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:08.073
CLARISSA WARD: Back in
Ghazni, our attempts

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:11.544
to see that justice system
in action are repeatedly

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:13.011
stonewalled.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.013
We're told that the
Sharia high court

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:18.784
is closed despite the
people waiting outside.

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:20.552
We're trying to show that
you have a judicial system.

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:21.754
[interposing voices]

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:24.323
As we try to persuade
the Taliban to let us in,

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:27.559
we see two men head
into the court.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:31.564
Our Taliban minder relents
and lets us follow them.

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.766
But in the courtroom,
the judge makes

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:36.135
it clear we are not welcome.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:38.370
- [non-english speech]

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:41.274
CLARISSA WARD: "Tell
them to stop." he says.

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:44.076
We are quickly ushered out.

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:47.813 line:8%
We've been trying all day to
get into the Sharia court.

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:50.483 line:8%
They're not letting us, but they
also won't give us a reason.

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:52.150 line:14%
- [non-english speech]

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:54.419 line:8%
CLARISSA WARD: It may be
that what happens behind

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.456 line:8%
closed doors here
doesn't fit the Taliban's

00:05:57.557 --> 00:06:01.093 line:14%
new carefully cultivated image.

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:03.763
And that the movement
born in conflict

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:07.032
is still brutal at its core.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:10.803
Clarissa Ward, CNN Ghazni.

